   ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\", \"      :\", \"      ,\",\n\n[P14] “我在这儿呢！”，\n\n[P15] 天渐渐黑下来。\n\n“蓝色啦，我看不清你了！”，\n\n[P16] “我在这儿呢！\n“戴上红帽子。”\n\n[P17] “哈，这下清楚了！”，\n\n[P18] 一起回家去。\n\n[P19] 毛毛虫美育馆\n《捉迷藏》延伸美术活动\n别躲啦\n红色啦，蓝色啦，你们都别再躲啦。\n材料准备：\n彩色纸、水彩笔。\n一、按图折若干个不同颜色的色啦纸偶。（图1系列15张步骤图）\n1-1. 取正方形纸。\n1-2. 对角线折成三角形。\n1-3-4-5. 打开，折成冰淇淋状。\n1-6. 第一次翻身。\n\n[P20] 1-7. 折一个倒三角形。\n1-8. 第二次翻身。\n1-9-10. 折出两个小三角形，色啦的后脑勺出现了。\n1-11. 头顶折平。\n1-12. 向上折三角形。\n1-13. 第三次翻身。\n1-14. 下巴折平。\n1-15. 折出双手，色啦雏形完成了。\n二、用水彩笔给色啦画上表情，让它站起来。（图2）\n三、把色啦纸偶摆放到色纸上，看看哪个色啦最明显，哪个色啦最隐蔽。（图3系列任选）\n\n[P21] 毛毛虫童书馆·第一辑\n《小蝌蚪找妈妈》\n《东郭先生》\n《老虎外婆》\n《金瓜银豆》\n《好乖乖》\n《九色鹿》\n《香蕉娃娃》\n\n毛毛虫童书馆·第四辑\n《中国童谣》\n《四季儿歌——春》\n《四季儿歌——夏》\n《四季儿歌——秋》\n《四季儿歌——冬》\n《传统童谣——小老鼠》\n《传统童谣——开城门》\n《传统童谣——不倒翁》\n《传统童谣——放风筝》\n\n毛毛虫童书馆·第二辑\n《胖嫂回娘家》\n《嫦娥奔月》\n《三十六个字》\n《三借芭蕉扇》\n《动物园》\n《春节的故事》\n\n毛毛虫童书馆·第五辑\n《中国传统节日故事》\n《春节的故事》\n《元宵节的故事》\n《二月二的故事》\n《端午节的故事》\n《七夕的故事》\n《中秋节的故事》\n《小年的故事》\n《腊八节的故事》\n\n毛毛虫童书馆·第三辑\n《聪明的乌龟》\n《两只老鼠胆子大》\n《小山羊和小老虎》\n《小猪奴尼》\n《雪狮子》\n\n毛毛虫童书馆·第六辑\n《颜色国的秘密》\n《彩蛋》\n《捉迷藏》\n《新被套》\n《干净小屋》\n《舞会皇后》\n《枫树的头饰》\n《两个好朋友》\n《我也很漂亮》\n《一幅抽象画》\n《明星哪去了》\n\n毛毛虫童书馆",
  "full_text_en": "[P1] Hide and Seek\nLianhuanhua Publishing House\n\n[P2] A Message to the Reader\nChildren, you've all played hide-and-seek, right?\nThis story is about Red and Blue playing hide-and-seek. But,\nthe places they hide are different from yours. Red hides in the red flowers,\nand Blue hides in the blue sea. Huh? They're gone!\nWhy is that?\nWell, they both hide in colors similar to themselves (this is called\n\"camouflage\"), so they're not easy to find.\nThere are many such examples in nature: flower butterflies resemble flowers,\nfrogs resemble leaves, fish in the sea resemble coral, white rabbits resemble snow,\nand octopuses can even change their color to match their surroundings.\nSmall animals also know how to use \"camouflage\" to protect themselves,\nplaying hide-and-seek with their enemies.\n\n[P3] Hide and Seek\nChen Qiuying, text\nHuang Yimin, illustrations\nLianhuanhua Publishing House\n\n[P4] Red La comes out to play.\n\n[P5] Blue La comes out to play too.\n\n[P6] \"Hello!\"\n\"Hello!\"\n\n[P7] Let's play hide and seek together.\n\n[P8] \"Red La, where are you?\"\n\n[P9] \"I'm here!\"\n\n[P10] \"It's my turn to hide!\"\n\n[P11] \"Goodbye!\"\n\n[P14] \"I'm here!\"\n\n[P15] The sky is gradually getting dark.\n\n\"Blue La, I can't see you clearly!\"\n\n[P16] \"I'm here!\"\n\"Put on the red hat.\"\n\n[P17] \"Ha, now I can see you clearly!\"\n\n[P18] Let's go home together.\n\n[P19] Caterpillar Art Gallery\nExtension Art Activity for 'Hide and Seek'\nDon't Hide Anymore\nRed La, Blue La, you both stop hiding now.\nMaterials needed:\nColored paper, watercolor pens.\n1. Fold several paper dolls of different colors according to the diagrams. (Diagram Series 1, 15 steps)\n1-1. Take a square piece of paper.\n1-2. Fold along the diagonal to form a triangle.\n1-3-4-5. Open it up and fold into an ice cream shape.\n1-6. First flip.\n\n[P20] 1-7. Fold an inverted triangle.\n1-8. Flip for the second time.\n1-9-10. Fold two small triangles; the back of the color character's head appears.\n1-11. Fold the top flat.\n1-12. Fold the triangle upward.\n1-13. Flip for the third time.\n1-14. Fold the chin flat.\n1-15. Fold out the hands; the basic shape of the color character is complete.\nTwo. Use watercolor pens to draw expressions on the color character and make it stand up. (Figure 2)\nThree. Place the color character paper dolls on colored paper and see which one is most visible and which one is most hidden. (Choose any from Figure 3 series)\n\n[P21] Caterpillar Children's Library · Volume 1\n《Little Tadpole Looking for Mom》\n《Mr. Dongguo》\n《Tiger Grandma》\n《Golden Gourd, Silver Bean》\n《Good Boy》\n《Nine-Colored Deer》\n《Banana Doll》\n\nCaterpillar Children's Library · Volume 4\n《Chinese Nursery Rhymes》\n《Four Seasons Rhymes — Spring》\n《Four Seasons Rhymes — Summer》\n《Four Seasons Rhymes — Autumn》\n《Four Seasons Rhymes — Winter》\n《Traditional Rhymes — Little Mouse》\n《Traditional Rhymes — Open the Gate》\n《Traditional Rhymes —不倒翁 (Inverted翁)》\n《Traditional Rhymes — Flying Kites》\n\nCaterpillar Children's Library · Volume 2\n《Fat Sister Returning Home》\n《Chang'e Flying to the Moon》\n《Thirty-Six Characters》\n《Borrowing the Banana Fan Three Times》\n《Zoo》\n《The Story of Spring Festival》\n\nCaterpillar Children's Library · Volume 5\n《Chinese Traditional Festival Stories》\n《The Story of Spring Festival》\n《The Story of Lantern Festival》\n《The Story of the Second Day of the Second Month》\n《The Story of Dragon Boat Festival》\n《The Story of Qixi》\n《The Story of Mid-Autumn Festival》\n《The Story of Xiao Nian》\n《The Story of Laba Festival》\n\nCaterpillar Children's Library · Volume 3\n《The Clever Turtle》\n《Two Mice with Big Courage》\n《Little Goat and Little Tiger》\n《Little Pig Nuni》\n《Snow Lion》\n\nCaterpillar Children's Library · Volume 6\n《The Secret of Color Land》\n《Colored Eggs》\n《Hide and Seek》\n《New Quilt Cover》\n《Clean Little House》\n《Ballroom Queen》\n《Maple Tree's Hair Accessory》\n《Two Good Friends》\n《I'm Also Very Beautiful》\n《An Abstract Painting》\n《Where Did the Star Go?》\n\nCaterpillar Children's Library",
  "full_summary_zh": "[P1] 本页为绘本封面，标题为《捉迷藏》，画面中央是一个戴着红色帽子的蓝色卡通角色，背景为蓝色并点缀着星星，底部标注出版社为连环画出版社。\n[P2] 本页是绘本的导读页，向小读者介绍故事内容：红色啦和蓝色啦通过与自身颜色相似的环境来玩捉迷藏，并引申到自然界中动物利用相似色（伪装）保护自己的现象。\n[P3] 本页为绘本《捉迷藏》的标题页，显示了书名、作者陈秋影、插画师黄毅民以及出版社连环画出版社的信息，页面四周有红蓝相间的抽象图案装饰。\n[P4] 红色啦戴着红色帽子，穿着红色衣服，从红色房子前的小路上走出来，准备出去玩。\n[P5] 蓝色啦从蓝色房子前的小路上走出来，准备出去玩。\n[P6] 红色啦和蓝色啦在画面中相遇，互相打招呼说“你好！”，并伸出手准备握手。\n[P7] 红色啦和蓝色啦站在一片红色花朵前，准备一起玩捉迷藏。\n[P8] 蓝色啦站在一片红色花朵前，正在寻找红色啦，画面中只有蓝色啦的对话，询问红色啦的位置。\n[P9] 红色啦藏在红色花朵中，从花丛里探出头来，喊出“我在这儿呢！”，向蓝色啦宣告自己的位置。\n[P10] 蓝色啦和红色啦在船上玩捉迷藏，蓝色啦说“该我藏了！”，准备开始新一轮游戏。\n[P11] 蓝色啦从红色船旁的海水中跃出，喊着“再见！”，似乎在告别或结束游戏。\n[P13] 红色啦站在一艘红白相间的船上，船在蓝色的水中航行，船尾留下波纹；旁边有一个红白蓝相间的救生圈在水中漂浮，救生圈后也有波纹，画面表现了船行水中的动态场景。\n[P14] 蓝色啦从红白相间的救生圈中探出头，微笑着喊出“我在这儿呢！”，似乎在回应红色啦的寻找或宣告自己的位置。\n[P15] 天色渐暗，红色啦站在星空下，对藏起来的蓝色啦说看不清对方了。\n[P16] 在星空下，红色啦举起一顶红帽子，喊着“我在这儿呢！”，并建议“戴上红帽子”，似乎在帮助蓝色啦在黑暗中被找到。\n[P17] 在星空下，蓝色啦戴着红色帽子，红色啦看着它，画面上方有对话文字“哈，这下清楚了！”，表明蓝色啦被找到了。\n[P18] 画面中有一红一蓝两座小房子，烟囱冒着烟，夜空中有星星，下方文字写着“一起回家去”，暗示红色啦和蓝色啦结束游戏，准备回家。\n[P19] 本页是《捉迷藏》故事的延伸美术活动，主题为“别躲啦”，指导孩子用彩色纸和水彩笔折出不同颜色的“色啦”纸偶，并展示了折纸的前几步步骤图。\n[P20] 本页展示了制作‘色啦’纸偶的折纸步骤，包括折叠、画表情和摆放观察对比，是《捉迷藏》故事的延伸美术活动。\n[P21] 本页展示了“毛毛虫童书馆”系列丛书的六辑书目列表，包括第一辑至第六辑的各册书名，页面底部有一个蓝色卡通角色在红白救生圈中的插图。"
}